XHR is installed as a loopback-only SOCKS5 client. It does not configure a
system proxy and it never enables itself automatically.

Copy the example configuration and add the deployment IDs and keys created
from the XHR deployment guide. The client supports one to five deployments in
the gas_urls array:

  install -Dm600 /usr/share/doc/xhr-client/examples/config.json \
    ~/.config/xhr-client/config.json
  editor ~/.config/xhr-client/config.json

Run it in a terminal:

  xhr-client

Or run it as a per-user systemd service:

  systemctl --user enable --now xhr-client

The listener defaults to 127.0.0.1:1080. Never put a real key in a bug report.
The desktop launcher uses the same XHR logo as the Android release and starts
the client in a terminal with that per-user configuration path.
